title The bound with two meters and no wall
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Lap index from git log --oneline | wc -l = 3373, so the council rota reads row 3373 mod 5 = 3 -- Water and Venus, care and flow: the shape you grew and the shape you are (Gall and Conway fused), the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. Conway landed directly on the lap: this organization is one durable person and a rotating population of agents who share a codebase and share no memory, so the written artifact outranks the clever arrangement, and construction/ITINERARY.md is the single highest-read written artifact that population has.
think The cold roster opened 50 guards, 50 green, 0 red, and every one of the 17 living REDS rows reads CLOSED. Standfast is satisfied, so the lap takes constructive work.
think The previous lap's recommend named the four-room index fold as the next crux and booked this card at 47,188 bytes against a 24,576 bound as its own round, writing that the condensing wants to become a habit with a measurement rather than an occasional sweep. Lindy-first settles between them: an index front door is read occasionally, this card is read first by every lap of the unattended loop.
think Measuring before condensing found the sharper half. living_docs_lint duty 6 named exactly two pages over the bound -- session-logs/README.md at 280,142 and construction/ITINERARY.md at 47,213 -- and those are the two documents the loop reads first every lap. Then the roster question: which guard REFUSES on that law? equinox_e123_living_pin_guard, over a hand-written roster of seven paths, with this card marked advisory and session-logs/README.md absent altogether. Duty 6 discovers sixty and by its own header always exits 0. Two meters, no wall.
think Grepping the declaration form gave the count that names the class: thirteen living pages write **Bound:** under living_pin_max_bytes in their own header, and one of them sits on the enforcing roster. That is REDS %187's shape a fourth time, and REDS %195 had already named the repair one lap earlier in a different room -- the DECLARATION is the thing to discover, since a page that writes down its own limit has told the tree what to measure it against.
think So the reading joins declared_ceiling rather than raising a third roof over one law. It is the same sentence one unit over: a page declares its own limit and something measures it. The number is read from the seated law at context/specs/20260724-132812 rather than copied a fourth time, and a page spelling a different number is gated at zero.
think Reading the law spec to wire that up found the second red. A plain grep -n over it returned nothing while cat showed the words plainly. Four more tracked text files carried the same fault -- a lone 0xC2, the lead byte of a middot whose continuation an earlier ASCII sweep replaced with a hyphen.
think My first reading of that was wrong and I caught it before building on it. I had written that every text meter in the tree was blind to those files. Measuring the actual binary showed GNU grep 3.12, which every script here runs, reads them correctly -- my interactive shell resolves grep to ugrep 7.8.4, which classifies them binary and returns silence. So no guard was blinded and a hand searching the tree was. The gate therefore reads UTF-8 validity rather than any one tool's verdict, since a gate written against a tool moves when the tool moves.
obs The condense lost a whole section and structure caught it. Cutting the three-doors paragraph spanned across ## Prior laps and swallowed it; checking the heading list against the departing card found it in one line. A card rewrite that only measures bytes cannot see a section that left.
obs Two duplications inside one card, both fused rather than trimmed. ## The order carried the same four equinoxes as ## The Compass Season, and ## The cadence carried a stale copy of the seed's four-gate reading -- copied=6789 where the custody-gates block beside it read 6,961. A card holding one fact twice is exactly the single-strandedness the card claims to keep.
obs Both walls proven to bite on the real tree rather than only in a pen: 4,000 bytes appended to the card, declared_ceiling refusing with over_declared_bound and naming the page and both numbers, equinox_e123 exiting 1, the card restored byte-identical by cmp.
obs Named rather than fixed: three scripts still carry their own 24576 -- living_docs_lint_scan.sh, equinox_e123_living_pin_guard_scan.sh, index_fold_scan.sh. Repointing them at the law the fourth now reads is its own lap.
obs session-logs/README.md stays over its declared bound at 282,139 bytes as this round ships (280,142 before this lap's own index row), and the honest reason is that its remedy is word-gated: rows fold when logs fold, and the log fold runs on Keaton's word. It rides a ceiling that only falls, surfaced as an open door rather than crossed.
obs The hot roster earned its place. Cold it read 50 of 50 green; run again after git add it read 49 of 50, with geode_libraries red because docs-geode/libraries/README.md counts witnesses BY REFERENCE and my own REDS rows had cited one more witness from construction/. Regenerated, restaged, and the roster run a third time so the green measures the tree the commit ships (REDS %174, %188).
